"""Walk-through of lesson 38, Design a URL Shortener.

Example numbers (mine, checked by script; they follow the section text): 100 million new links a month = about 40 writes a second;
100 opens per link = 4,000 redirects a second, peaks near 12,000; five years = 6 billion links x 500 bytes = 3 TB.
7 base-62 characters = 62^7 = about 3.5 trillion codes; the first clash is expected after about 2 million links = 50,000 s at 40/s, under 14 hours.
A scraper at 1,000 requests a second walks 6 billion counter codes in 69 days; random codes: 1 guess in 587 hits a real link, and the whole space takes 111 years.
Cache with a 90% hit rate: 4,000 reads a second become 400 (peak 12,000 -> 1,200). 3 TB over 30 partitions = 100 GB each, 3 copies = 9 TB of disk.
Clicks: 20,000 events in a 5 s window over 2,000 links = 400 writes a second instead of 4,000. A spammer at 5,000 links a minute is 2.08x the normal 2,400 a minute; a limit of 10 a minute is 500x fewer.
"""
